NETGROUP_MKDB(8)          BSD System Manager's Manual         NETGROUP_MKDB(8)

NNAAMMEE
     nneettggrroouupp__mmkkddbb — generate the netgroup databases

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     nneettggrroouupp__mmkkddbb [--oo _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e] [_f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     nneettggrroouupp__mmkkddbb creates Berkeley databases for the specified _f_i_l_e.  If no
     file is specified, _/_e_t_c_/_n_e_t_g_r_o_u_p is used.  These databases are then in‐
     stalled into _/_e_t_c_/_n_e_t_g_r_o_u_p_._d_b.  The file must be in the correct format
     (see netgroup(5)).

     The options are as follows:

     --oo _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e
             Put the output databases in the named file.

     The databases are used by the C library netgroup routines (see
     getnetgrent(3)).

FFIILLEESS
     /etc/netgroup.db          current netgroup database
     /etc/netgroup.db.tmp      a temporary file
     /etc/netgroup             current netgroup file

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The nneettggrroouupp__mmkkddbb utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     dbopen(3), getnetgrent(3), netgroup(5)

BBUUGGSS
     Because nneettggrroouupp__mmkkddbb guarantees not to install a partial destination
     file, it must build a temporary file in the same file system and if suc‐
     cessful use rename(2) to install over the destination file.

     If nneettggrroouupp__mmkkddbb fails, it will leave the previous version of the desti‐
     nation file intact.

